-- title:
--   Integrality of 1/wₚ(j) over R[1/j] up to a unit
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime with $p\nmid N$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p)` for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the set of Laurent series $j(q^d) =$ `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the positive divisors $d$ of $Np$, where `jq` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`. Let $R$ be a commutative ring with algebra structures on $\mathbb{Q}$ and on $F$ forming a scalar tower $R\to\mathbb{Q}\to F$, let $J\in F$ be the element given by `jq` itself, and let $A =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {J⁻¹}` be the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $J^{-1}$. Finally let $\sigma =$ `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N p` be the chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ interchanging $j(q^d)$ and $j(q^{dp})$ for every positive divisor $d$ of $N$ (the identity if no such automorphism exists). The assertion is that there exists $a\in A$ such that the element $(1 + J^{-1}a)\cdot \sigma(J)^{-1}$ of $F$ is integral over $A$.
--
--   This is the local statement at the cusps needed to extend the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ of $X_0(Np)$ over a base ring $R$: on the chart $j\neq 0$ of the normalisation of the $j$-line in $F$, the function $1/w_p(j)$ becomes integral over $R[1/j]$ after inverting a single element congruent to $1$ modulo $1/j$. It is used in the construction of the involution on the integral model, in [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_iso_involutive_iotaFin_comp_eq_atkinLehner_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_iso_involutive_iotaFin_comp_eq_atkinLehner_of_not_dvd).
